# 📊 HR Analytics Dashboard

## 👨‍💻 Project Overview

The HR Analytics Dashboard is a data visualization project developed using Microsoft Power BI.

The main objective of this project is to analyze employee data and understand workforce performance, employee attrition, employee distribution, and HR-related metrics.

This dashboard helps HR teams and business managers understand employee trends and make better data-driven decisions.

## 🎯 Project Objectives

- Analyze total employee count.
- Understand employee attrition.
- Calculate employee attrition rate.
- Analyze employee age distribution.
- Identify employee attrition by department.
- Analyze employee attrition by job role.
- Compare employee attrition by gender.
- Understand employee monthly income.
- Identify workforce trends and patterns.

## 🛠️ Tools & Technologies

- Microsoft Power BI
- Power Query
- DAX
- Excel
- Data Visualization
- Data Analysis

## 📊 Dashboard Preview

![HR Analytics Dashboard](./Hr%20Analytics%20Dashboard.png)

## 📌 Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)

### 1. Total Employees

Displays the total number of employees available in the organization.

### 2. Total Attrition

Shows the number of employees who left the organization.

### 3. Attrition Rate

Represents the percentage of employees who left the organization compared to the total employee population.

### 4. Average Age

Displays the average age of employees in the organization.

### 5. Average Monthly Income

Shows the average monthly income of employees.

### 6. Average Years at Company

Represents the average number of years employees have worked in the organization.

## 📈 Dashboard Visualizations

### Employee Attrition by Department

Analyzes employee attrition across different departments.

### Employee Attrition by Job Role

Identifies which job roles have higher employee attrition.

### Employee Attrition by Age Group

Helps understand employee attrition patterns across different age groups.

### Employee Attrition by Gender

Compares employee attrition between male and female employees.

### Employee Attrition by Education Field

Analyzes employee attrition based on educational background.

### Employee Attrition by Years at Company

Helps understand the relationship between employee experience and attrition.

### Employee Attrition by Monthly Income

Analyzes employee attrition across different income levels.

## 🔍 Key Insights

- The dashboard provides an overview of employee workforce distribution.
- It helps identify departments experiencing employee attrition.
- Job role analysis helps understand employee turnover patterns.
- Age group analysis provides insights into employee retention.
- Gender-based analysis helps compare workforce attrition.
- Monthly income analysis helps explore compensation-related patterns.
- Employee experience analysis helps understand workforce stability.

## 🧹 Data Preparation

The project includes data preparation and transformation using Power Query.

The preparation process involves:

1. Importing employee data.
2. Checking column names and data types.
3. Identifying missing values.
4. Checking duplicate records.
5. Preparing data for analysis.
6. Creating calculated metrics.
7. Loading the prepared data into Power BI.

## 📊 Data Analysis

The dashboard uses employee data to analyze workforce metrics.

The analysis focuses on:

- Employee distribution.
- Employee attrition.
- Job role analysis.
- Department analysis.
- Employee demographics.
- Employee income.
- Employee experience.

## 💡 Business Benefits

This dashboard helps organizations:

- Monitor workforce performance.
